\section{Phenomenology}
\label{sec:phenomenology}

The analysis of the previous sections puts us in position to now discuss the phenomenology
of the $X$ boson.  To do this, we  first detail the relevant interactions it has with the SM gauge bosons. 

\begin{figure}[t]
  \centering
  \includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{diagram-vertex-xzz} 
  \caption{$\Gamma_{XZZ}$ and $\Gamma_{XZ\gamma}$ interaction vertices, generated by~(\ref{eq:15})}
