\subsection{Decays of $X$ boson}

The $X$ boson decays primarily via its couplings to SM gauge boson pairs.  The  important decay channels are computed from the interaction vertices computed above.
The corresponding decay widths are:
\begin{align}
  \Gamma_{X\to ZZ} & = \frac{\bc1^2 \ssw M_X^3}{192\pi M_Z^2} \left(1-\frac{4
      M_Z^2}{M_X^2}\right)^{5/2} \approx \bc1^2\, (45\gev)
  \left(\frac{M_X}{\mathrm{TeV}}\right)^3 +
  \ldots
  , \nonumber \\
  \Gamma_{X\to W^+W^-} & = \frac{\bc2^2 M_X^3}{48\pi M_W^2}\left(1-\frac{4
      M_W^2}{M_X^2}\right)^{5/2} \label{eq:41} \approx \bc2^2\,
  (1.03\;\mathrm{TeV})\left(\frac{M_X}{\mathrm{TeV}}\right)^3 +\ldots\\

  \Gamma_{X\to Z\gamma} & = \frac{\bc1^2 \ccw M_X^3}{96\pi M_Z^2}
  \left(1-\frac{
      M_Z^2}{M_X^2}\right)^3\left(1+\frac{M_Z^2}{M_X^2}\right)\approx \bc1^2\,
  (307\gev) \left(\frac{M_X}{\mathrm{TeV}}\right)^3 +\ldots,

  ,\nonumber
\end{align}
where $\dots$ denote corrections of the order $(M_V/M_X)^2$. The interaction
term of eq.~(\ref{eq:15}) also allows interaction of the $X$ boson with
$\gamma H$ and $ZH$, which are generically small.

